      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "The question requires µmol/kg while CMIP6 no3 and po4 are stored per unit volume, and this fragment says the conversion scale differs by variable and from observational mass units.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`no3`/`po4` are archived in mol m-3; convert to µmol kg-1 with µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ, where ρ is in kg m-3. The question prescribes a constant ρ = 1025 kg/m3; the fragment prefers the in-situ density for anything below the surface, so state that the constant-density assumption was used (`attrs['density_assumption']`).",
        "N:P is a ratio of two tracers put on the mass basis with the same ρ, so it is scale-invariant and needs no conversion; only the µmol kg-1 regression does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The model-versus-WOA23 N:P comparison and basin statistics exist only where fields share valid data, so this fragment constrains the common mask and cell-wise comparison.",
      "status": "not_applicable",
      "not_applicable_reason": "the question asks each source's own means and regression over its own valid cells, not a cell-by-cell model–observation score on one shared mask."
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The question uses the WOA23 basin mask with Pacific, Atlantic and Indian Oceans excluding Southern and Arctic, and this fragment says basin statistics depend on the chosen partition and must state it.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Take basins from the WOA23 mask with `select_basin` and `include_marginal_seas=True` (marginal seas folded into their parent ocean); state that this is a WOA labelling, not the OMIP 10-region one, and that the Southern and Arctic Oceans are separate basins (excluded here).",
        "`depth_dependent=False` applies the surface labels through the whole column — what a named ocean usually means; with `depth_dependent=True` a marginal sea's label stops at its sill, so the two choices give different 200–1000 m basin means."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "The question supplies each model’s volcello and asks for percentages of water volume, and this fragment defines volcello as tracer-cell volume.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The layer thickness that respects partial bottom cells is `volcello` / `areacello` (`cell_thickness_like`), not `lev_bnds` differences: the two differ by more than 1 % in 14 % of GFDL-ESM4 cells and by up to ±50 % in 3.3 % of MPI-ESM1-2-LR cells.",
        "Use each model's own `volcello` as the volume weight and report `attrs['volume_source']` alongside the numbers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The percentage-of-water-volume calculations require volume weighting over all ocean cells, which this fragment specifies.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Volume-weight every mean over the 200–1000 m layer (`op='volume_weighted_mean'`), restricting the weights to the same valid cells; take the percentage of volume with N:P between 14 and 18, and below 12, from `compute_exceedance_fraction` and report the m3 behind each percentage.",
        "The mean of a ratio is not the ratio of the means: `compute_ratio` gives the cell-by-cell N:P (the headline value); the ratio of the volume-weighted mean `no3` to the volume-weighted mean `po4` is a differently weighted quantity, so both are labelled as the question asks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "bgc-model-structure-comparison",
      "severity": "info",
      "path": "datasets/bgc-model-structure-comparison.md",
      "sha256": "4ef3e4ab0b9741f6ab5d15f88cfbdf8b7366c82b093ce99e26f1707a2a788e54",
      "reason": "Interpreting any low-N:P or denitrification signal across CESM2, GFDL-ESM4 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR requires accounting for their different stoichiometry, DOM pools and N2 fixation.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Interpret cross-model N:P spread as partly structural: fixed N:P per plankton type in GFDL-ESM4, prescribed Redfield organic matter in MPI-ESM1-2-LR, variable C:P in CESM2; \"not detailed in paper\" does not mean the feature is absent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "Figure 2 requires putting curvilinear model fields on a regular grid for display, and this fragment says regridding changes masks and conservation, so integrals and comparisons should be done natively and regridding used only for maps.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute every number (means, ratio of means, exceedance fractions) on each source's own grid with its own areas and volumes; regrid to a regular longitude–latitude grid for Figure 2 only, with 'conservative' for model fields and 'nearest_s2d' for categorical masks, and state the method.",
        "Integrate the 200–1000 m layer thickness-weighted on the original levels; vertical interpolation onto another level set changes layer-integrated quantities and is for comparison, not budgets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The 1971–2000 climatologies are built from monthly CMIP6 means, and N:P is nonlinear, so this fragment warns that offline ratios of monthly means can differ from the mean of the diagnostic.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build the 1971–2000 climatology with `temporal_aggregate(freq='mean')`, which weights by calendar month length; an equal-weight `op='mean'` over time is not a time average.",
        "N:P is nonlinear, so the ratio is formed on each month's field and then averaged (diagnostic first, then average); state this order, since average-then-ratio is the diagnostic of the mean state."
      ]
